description:
Objective: an operator-invoked `node scripts/local-runner/cli.mjs certify --work-dir <absolute path>`. It runs the real isolation flow on this host's own platform module and writes one fixed-schema evidence report. That report is the ONLY evidence that can establish an isolation support claim (CQ-R13 DoD 1). The human decided in the architect REPL on 2026-10-30:
- an agent builds it;
- the human runs it on Windows, Linux and macOS hardware and attaches the reports;
- CQ-R13 completes only once all three pass.
It never enables verified-local.

Split out of CQ-R13 (task-f4811a72) by architect-e4b7eee0 on 2026-10-30. It depends on CQ-R13a, which edits cli.mjs and local-runner.test.mjs first. Later rows append checks to the registry this row lands: CQ-R13e (bridge and network), CQ-R13f (containment), CQ-R13h (cancellation and recovery) and CQ-R13g (canary check).

Model: native-smoke.mjs.
- The injectable core's evidence is always transport 'injected' and can never certify.
- The native entry takes exactly { workDir } and uses platformFor(process.platform).
- Unlike the smoke, it installs the REAL guest-supervisor.py bytes and a fresh random credential, because later checks need the real supervisor.

Deliverable — a new scripts/local-runner/certify.mjs:
- CERTIFY_CHECKS, a frozen, ordered registry of {id, run}. This row lands four checks:
  - 'provision': provisionGuest through the host platform;
  - 'readiness': bootstrapReady with failures === []. It records the guest's exact cloud-init status. R07's QA note on CQ-R13 says a clean real boot must reach done/done, and degraded is a failure;
  - 'no-mounts': assertNoMounts;
  - 'teardown': deleteOwned of exactly this run's VM, after which the ledger holds no live record of this run's attempt.
- The checks run in order and share one context ({ name, platform, provider, ledger, owner, ... }). After a failure, every later check except 'teardown' is 'not-run'. Teardown always runs, even after a throw.
- Report, frozen: {kind:'isolation-certification', version:1, platform, arch, transport, provider:{executable, version}, image:{sourceSha256, providerImageHash}, supervisorSha256, startedAt, finishedAt, checks:[{id, result, code}], certified, executionReady:false}.
  - result is 'passed', 'failed' or 'not-run'; code is a fixed code or null.
  - certified = transport === 'native' && every registry check passed.
  - Only fixed codes appear, never a path, the credential or a guest byte.
- The native run writes the JSON report to <workDir>/certification-<platform>-<arch>-<UTC stamp>.json, opened O_EXCL with mode 0600, and returns it.
- An export validateCertificationReport(value) returns the frozen report when value has exactly this schema, with every check id of the current registry in order. Otherwise it throws CERTIFY_REPORT_INVALID. CQ-R13 uses it to check the operator's attached reports.
- cli.mjs gains a `certify --work-dir <absolute path>` command, parsed like native-smoke and lazily imported. It exits 0 only when certified === true.
- local-runner-bundle.test.mjs: `required` gains certify.mjs.

Tests, in scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs, run the injected core with a fake provider. The native run itself is operator-only, never CI. They cover:
- injected evidence never certifies, even when every check passes;
- check order, 'not-run' after a failure, and teardown always running and deleting only this run's VM;
- the exact report schema, with no secret in it;
- validateCertificationReport accepting and refusing exactly;
- the native entry refusing anything but { workDir } (CERTIFY_INPUT_INVALID) and an unsupported host (CERTIFY_UNSUPPORTED_HOST);
- the report file being created O_EXCL with mode 0600.

Out of scope:
- the bridge, containment, cancellation, recovery and canary checks (the later rows);
- enabling verified-local or executionReady;
- .moe edits.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs (on WSL: env -i with the nvm Node 24 PATH)
